commit 32ab800164dc20801611f0d9764ea5365c791d36

C03: the observed title is not a copied instruction, title checks fold accents, yt-dlp prints UTF-8 and playback verification waits thirty seconds (MUSIC1561)

MUSIC1559 measured four provider-less music literals played and named by their observed title, and three finals lost: the retry hint names the observed title and the copied-instruction echo check took «ft. Julian Casablancas» for a copied fragment; yt-dlp delivered «Último» in the console code page («�ltimo») so the exact title check refused the draft; and a two-and-a-half-hour mix did not reach its first half second inside the adapter's 12,5 s window. llm.py exempts fragments that are observed values from the echo check and folds accents in both title checks; YouTubeMpvAdapter passes --encoding utf-8 to yt-dlp and polls up to 120 × 250 ms. Registry-wide recogniser diff: no literal changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


